{%- comment -%}
  PG Case Mobile: make the spare-case upsell tile fit a phone.

  pg-mobile builds `.pgx-case` as a single non-wrapping flex row: 52px thumb,
  text, price, then an ADD button padded 11px 26px. On a 390px screen the button
  and thumb take their width first, leaving the text roughly 110px, so "Add a
  spare protective case" breaks over three lines, the sentence below it turns
  into a tall ribbon, and the price ends up wedged against the button.

  Below 600px the tile becomes two rows instead:

      [thumb] [title + note............]
      [$13.99]              [   ADD   ]

  The text gets the full width beside the thumb, and the price and button share
  a second row with the button taking the slack, which also makes it a much
  bigger tap target. Rules are id-scoped and this section loads after pg-mobile,
  so they win on source order without fighting anything.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
@media (max-width:600px){
  #pgx .pgx-case{
    flex-wrap:wrap !important;
    gap:10px 12px !important;
    padding:14px !important;
    align-items:center !important
  }
  #pgx .pgx-case img{
    width:48px !important;height:48px !important;flex:none !important
  }
  /* flex-basis over half the row forces the price and button onto row two */
  #pgx .pgx-case-t{
    flex:1 1 60% !important;min-width:0 !important
  }
  #pgx .pgx-case-t b{font-size:15px !important;line-height:1.3 !important}
  #pgx .pgx-case-t small{font-size:12.5px !important;line-height:1.4 !important;margin-top:3px !important}
  #pgx .pgx-case-p{
    order:3 !important;flex:0 0 auto !important;font-size:16px !important
  }
  #pgx .pgx-case-add{
    order:4 !important;flex:1 1 auto !important;
    padding:13px 20px !important;font-size:13.5px !important
  }
}
</style>
{%- comment -%}
  ============================================================
  ADDED 2026-09-06. Host for the R36S / cart round of fixes
  below. It lives here rather than in its own section because
  registering a NEW section means rewriting the auto-generated
  sections/footer-group.json, which this session had no safe way
  to push. pg-case-mobile was the right host anyway: it is
  already wired into footer-group at position 14, so it renders
  AFTER every overlay-group cart section (pg-drawer, pg-giftguard,
  pg-cart-*) and after the PDP template sections, and it already
  owns the spare-case upsell. Verified: no later footer-group
  section touches .pg-tadd, .pgx-lad-chip, .pgx-tile-sub,
  .pgx-deal-note, .pgx-sstrike, .pg-sell-slot, .pgx-sellout,
  .sticky-in-panel or aside#cart.
  ============================================================

  PG R36S Fix (2026-09-06). Four reported problems, all measured on the live
  theme at 375px before anything was changed:

  1. "50% OFF TODAY" LOOKED RANDOM. Not the SAVE n% badge - that one is fine
     where it is, at the tile's top-right, and is left alone. The problem was
     .pgx-tile-sub, which rendered as the LAST line of the tile, under the
     "+ FREE Case" chip (measured: name 801, chip 858, sub 885), so the one
     line stating the actual offer hung off the bottom with nothing to relate
     to. The chip is markup inside .pgx-tile-name rather than a sibling, so
     CSS ordering cannot reach it; subFirst() moves the chip node to sit after
     the sub instead. Reads name -> 50% OFF today -> + FREE Case.

  2. SPARE-CASE ADD-ON ROW WAS TOO SMALL. .pg-tadd measured 34px tall on mobile
     (padding 5/7, 22px thumb, 10.5px label) - a checkbox-sized strip under a
     55px Add to cart button. Enlarged to ~46px on both the single and the duo
     tile. Scoped with :not(.pg-tadd-frame) so the lenticular poster's frame
     row, which already has its own larger sizing, is untouched.

  3. SELLOUT RISK CARD TOUCHED THE REVIEW UNDER IT. Measured: .pg-sell-slot
     bottom 1355, .pgx-quote top 1355. Exactly zero gap. pg-sellout-last sets
     margin:14px 0 0 on the slot, so there was top spacing and no bottom
     spacing. 18px added below.

  4. CART: THE FREE CASE COULD SHOW A PRICE, AND THE TWO CASE LINES SWAPPED
     IDENTITIES. This is the real bug and it is worth spelling out.

     Both cases are variants of ONE product, r36s-protective-case-free-gift:
     49640846426340 is the $0.00 gift, 49640879063268 is the $13.99 spare.
     Every existing script decides which cart line is "the free one" by
     POSITION, not by variant:

       - pg-drawer badge(): giftAt falls back to "the first line whose product
         link contains free-gift" whenever FREE_IDX/GIFT_IDX are not resolved
         yet - which is exactly the window right after a paid case is added.
       - pg-mobile caseLine(): shows .pg-free-tag when seen === 1, i.e. purely
         first-in-DOM-order, and force-sets visibility:visible !important on
         .semantic-amount / .nc-lsave / .price for EVERY case line, overriding
         the stylesheet rule that keeps money off the gift line.

     Cart line order is add order, and the paid case is frequently added FIRST:
     pg-theme-css's ride-along posts the add-on 900ms after Add to cart, while
     pg-giftguard only places the gift on its own 1200ms beat. Verified live:
     adding the spare case and the console together produced cart order
     [Spare case, Free with console, Console]. In that order both scripts above
     put FREE GIFT on the PAID line and leave the genuinely free line showing
     $12.59 / Save 50% - "the free case is showing that it costs them money".

     Also verified: pg-drawer's GIFT_ID and pg-mobile's CASE_VARIANT are both
     49623692247268, which no longer exists - POST /cart/add.js returns
     422 "Cannot find variant". So pg-drawer's giftSync cannot place the gift
     (pg-giftguard does it instead), and its "split the extra units onto a paid
     line" branch drops those units on the floor.

     The fix below settles identity by VARIANT ID, read from the line's own
     /cart/change?id=<variant>:<key> remove link - that link survives
     pgNoAddonLinks, which strips only hrefs containing r36s-protective-case.
     It re-asserts every 250ms because the drawer rebuilds its lines and
     one-shot guards lose to rebuilders. Result, always: one FREE GIFT line at
     $0.00 and one ordinary paid line, whatever order they were added in.

     Removing the misplaced pill is NOT enough on its own - pg-drawer re-adds
     it every 800ms and the two beats produce a visibly flickering badge. The
     paid line is stamped data-pg-paidcase and the pill is benched by rule (see
     4a), so it never paints even in the window between ticks.

  4b. TOGGLING SHIPPING PROTECTION MADE THE FREE-CASE TEXT GLITCH (2026-09-10).

     Reported: flick the Shipping Protection switch and the free case's text
     jumps around before settling. It is not the switch - it is what the switch
     does. pg-drawer's spBox() handler ends in spRefreshDrawer(), which
     re-fetches `/` and does

         cur.innerHTML = fresh.innerHTML;

     i.e. it replaces the WHOLE drawer with the server's rendering. Everything
     the pass below stamps onto a case line is DOM state and dies with it: the
     data-pg-case / data-pg-truefree / data-pg-paidcase attributes, the inline
     display:none on the variant paragraph, the hidden stepper, our own pill.

     And every rule in 4a was keyed on those attributes. So between the swap and
     the next 250ms tick the line rendered raw - the "Free with console /"
     variant line back, a stepper and a price on a $0.00 line - while
     pg-drawer's badge() (800ms) and pg-mobile's caseLine() (1200ms) each got a
     say on which line wears FREE GIFT. Three writers repainting one line at
     three different offsets is exactly the flicker, and it repeats on every
     toggle because every toggle rebuilds the drawer.

     Reproduced in Chromium against all three writers at their real beats: on
     the old rules every sampled frame from t+0 to t+2600ms after a rebuild was
     wrong in some way -- raw variant line and stepper for the first ~250ms, the
     FREE GIFT pill landing on the PAID line at t+120, the stepper flashing back
     at t+900 when pg-mobile's beat lands, and the struck $24.99 never hidden at
     all. On the rules below, every one of those frames is correct, including
     t+0 and t+16 -- before any script has run.

     THE ANSWER IS TO STOP DEPENDING ON THE STAMP. The rules below now key on
     markup the SERVER renders, so they are already in force in the same frame
     the new HTML lands, with no JS in the path:

       - any case line at all: `li:has(a[href*="free-gift"])` - both variants
         share that handle, so this benches a foreign pill on either of them.
       - the gift line specifically: `li:has(a[href*="id=49640846426340"])` -
         the remove link carries the variant id, which is the same evidence
         variantOf() reads, and it is in the server's HTML.

     The attribute selectors are kept alongside them: they are the fallback
     where :has() is unsupported, and for a line whose remove link is missing.

     THE PRICE IS HIDDEN WITH PROPERTIES pg-mobile DOES NOT WRITE. caseLine()
     sets `visibility:visible !important` INLINE on .semantic-amount, .nc-lsave,
     .cols, .money and .price for every case line, and inline !important beats
     any stylesheet rule - so a visibility-only hide is reversed on its beat and
     restored on ours, forever. opacity and pointer-events are not in its list
     (nor in pg-chips' STYLE map), so the same trick 4a already uses for the
     pills is used here for the money: the box keeps its size, the digits do not
     paint, and no other script can bring them back.

     pass() also runs the instant the drawer mutates now, not just on the
     250ms beat, so our own pill lands with the rest of the new markup rather
     than a fifth of a second later.

  5. MOBILE CART: 40px of dead white under CHECKOUT. Measured at 375x812:
     checkout button bottom 772, viewport 812. aside#cart carries a 34px
     bottom padding from the base theme (safe-area-inset-bottom is 0 here, so
     it is a literal), and .sticky-in-panel adds 6px. The sticky pane sticks to
     the bottom of the drawer's CONTENT box, so those 34px sat below it as bare
     white. pg-drawer's pgPane() owns that value and re-writes it inline every
     800ms, so it is changed there (34px -> 6px) rather than fought from here;
     the safe-area-inset moves INTO the pane's own padding. Net: the pane and
     its button drop ~28px, the gap under the button becomes 12px, and notched
     phones still clear the home indicator.

  6. "BUNDLE PRICING SHOWN" ON A SINGLE. See dealNote() below: pg-tile-copy
     prints one constant sentence under Add to Cart on this product, so a
     shopper with SINGLE selected was told bundle pricing was being shown. The
     first sentence is dropped for that tier only.

  7. SINGLE TILE SHOWED THE 64G COMPARE-AT ON 128G. See strikeSync() below:
     $129.99 struck against $74.99 (42%) next to a SAVE 50% badge, when the
     128G's real compare-at is $149.99. Read live from the product JSON.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  /* ---- 1. "50% OFF today" sits above the FREE Case chip ----
     The SAVE n% badge at the tile's top-right is deliberate and stays put.
     The chip becomes a block on its own line, which is the same treatment
     pg-tile-copy already gives it on ladder tiles. */
  #pgx#pgx .pgx-tile:not(.pgx-lad) .pgx-lad-chip{
    display:block !important;
    width:max-content !important;
    margin:5px 0 0 !important;
    vertical-align:baseline !important;
  }

  /* ---- 2. spare-case add-on row, both tiles ---- */
  #pgx#pgx .pg-tadd:not(.pg-tadd-frame){
    gap:10px !important;
    padding:9px 11px !important;
    border-radius:12px !important;
  }
  #pgx#pgx .pg-tadd:not(.pg-tadd-frame) img{
    width:32px !important;
    height:32px !important;
    border-radius:8px !important;
  }
  #pgx#pgx .pg-tadd:not(.pg-tadd-frame) .pg-tadd-ck{
    width:18px !important;
    height:18px !important;
    border-radius:5px !important;
  }
  #pgx#pgx .pg-tadd:not(.pg-tadd-frame) .pg-tadd-t{font-size:12.5px !important}
  #pgx#pgx .pg-tadd:not(.pg-tadd-frame) .pg-tadd-p{font-size:14px !important}
  #pgx#pgx .pg-tadd:not(.pg-tadd-frame) .pg-tadd-p s{font-size:11.5px !important}
  @media (max-width:600px){
    #pgx#pgx .pg-tadd:not(.pg-tadd-frame){
      gap:9px !important;
      padding:8px 10px !important;
    }
    #pgx#pgx .pg-tadd:not(.pg-tadd-frame) img{width:30px !important;height:30px !important}
    #pgx#pgx .pg-tadd:not(.pg-tadd-frame) .pg-tadd-t{font-size:12px !important}
    #pgx#pgx .pg-tadd:not(.pg-tadd-frame) .pg-tadd-p{font-size:13px !important}
    #pgx#pgx .pg-tadd:not(.pg-tadd-frame) .pg-tadd-p s{font-size:11px !important}
  }

  /* ---- 3. breathing room under the sellout-risk card, every PDP ---- */
  #pgx#pgx .pg-sell-slot{margin-bottom:18px !important}
  #pgx#pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-sellout{margin-bottom:18px !important}

  /* ---- 4. ONE gift pill, ours, on the line we choose ----
     pg-drawer's badge() ADDS .pg-free-tag to whichever case line it guessed
     and REMOVES it from every other one, on an 800ms beat. Fighting that node
     is unwinnable in BOTH directions: re-adding it on the right line flickers,
     and stripping it off the wrong line flickers. That is what the shopper
     sees as "the free gift logo glitching".

     So .pg-free-tag is benched on every case line and the badge is rendered as
     our own element, .pg-truegift-tag, which pg-drawer has never heard of and
     so never touches. One writer, no race.

     Benched with position/visibility/opacity/pointer-events rather than
     display, because pg-chips' stamp() writes its STYLE map - which contains
     display:inline-flex - onto .pg-free-tag, .pg-save-chip and .nc-lsave-off
     as INLINE !important every 300ms, and inline !important beats any
     stylesheet rule. Those four properties are the ones stamp() never writes;
     nc-linesave already benches .pg-save-chip exactly this way. Anything added
     to pg-chips' STYLE map later must stay clear of them.

     THE SELECTOR IS THE SERVER'S MARKUP, NOT OUR STAMP - see 4b. A case line
     is one whose product link carries the shared `free-gift` handle, which is
     true the moment the drawer's HTML is replaced and does not wait for a
     tick. The data-attribute selectors stay as the no-:has() fallback. */
  #cart#cart .l4ca > li:has(a[href*="free-gift"]) .pg-free-tag,
  #cart#cart .l4ca > li:has(a[href*="free-gift"]) .pg-free-sub,
  #cart#cart .l4ca > li[data-pg-case] .pg-free-tag,
  #cart#cart .l4ca > li[data-pg-case] .pg-free-sub,
  #cart#cart .l4ca > li[data-pg-truefree] .pg-free-note,
  #cart#cart .l4ca > li[data-pg-truefree] .nc-lsave-off,
  #cart#cart .l4ca > li[data-pg-truefree] .nc-lsave-was,
  #cart#cart .l4ca > li[data-pg-truefree] .pg-save-chip,
  body.template-cart .l4ca > li:has(a[href*="free-gift"]) .pg-free-tag,
  body.template-cart .l4ca > li:has(a[href*="free-gift"]) .pg-free-sub,
  body.template-cart .l4ca > li[data-pg-case] .pg-free-tag,
  body.template-cart .l4ca > li[data-pg-case] .pg-free-sub,
  body.template-cart .l4ca > li[data-pg-truefree] .pg-free-note,
  body.template-cart .l4ca > li[data-pg-truefree] .nc-lsave-off,
  body.template-cart .l4ca > li[data-pg-truefree] .nc-lsave-was,
  body.template-cart .l4ca > li[data-pg-truefree] .pg-save-chip{
    position:absolute !important;
    visibility:hidden !important;
    opacity:0 !important;
    pointer-events:none !important;
  }

  /* ---- 4b. THE GIFT LINE, RECOGNISED FROM THE SERVER'S HTML ----
     The remove link carries the variant id (/cart/change?id=<variant>:<key>),
     the same evidence variantOf() reads below, so the $0.00 line can be styled
     before any script has run - which is what stops the rebuild after a
     Shipping Protection toggle from flashing the raw line.

     The struck value, the save chips and the stepper are hidden with opacity
     and pointer-events as well as visibility: pg-mobile's caseLine() writes
     `visibility:visible !important` INLINE on these very elements every 1200ms,
     and inline beats a stylesheet. It does not write opacity. */
  #cart#cart .l4ca > li:has(a[href*="id=49640846426340"]) section > p:not([class]),
  body.template-cart .l4ca > li:has(a[href*="id=49640846426340"]) section > p:not([class]){
    display:none !important;
  }
  #cart#cart .l4ca > li:has(a[href*="id=49640846426340"]) .semantic-amount,
  #cart#cart .l4ca > li:has(a[href*="id=49640846426340"]) .nc-lsave-was,
  #cart#cart .l4ca > li:has(a[href*="id=49640846426340"]) .nc-lsave-off,
  #cart#cart .l4ca > li:has(a[href*="id=49640846426340"]) .pg-save-chip,
  #cart#cart .l4ca > li[data-pg-truefree] .semantic-amount,
  body.template-cart .l4ca > li:has(a[href*="id=49640846426340"]) .semantic-amount,
  body.template-cart .l4ca > li:has(a[href*="id=49640846426340"]) .nc-lsave-was,
  body.template-cart .l4ca > li:has(a[href*="id=49640846426340"]) .nc-lsave-off,
  body.template-cart .l4ca > li:has(a[href*="id=49640846426340"]) .pg-save-chip,
  body.template-cart .l4ca > li[data-pg-truefree] .semantic-amount{
    visibility:hidden !important;
    opacity:0 !important;
    pointer-events:none !important;
  }

  /* pg-drawer pins `li:has(.pg-free-tag)` to the top with order:-1. With the
     pill on the paid line, the PAID case was being pinned above the gift -
     visible in the report. Ordering is stated explicitly instead, and from the
     server's markup too so the rows do not re-sort a beat after a rebuild. */
  #cart#cart .l4ca > li:has(a[href*="id=49640846426340"]){order:-1 !important}
  #cart#cart .l4ca > li:has(a[href*="id=49640879063268"]){order:0 !important}
  #cart#cart .l4ca > li[data-pg-truefree]{order:-1 !important}
  #cart#cart .l4ca > li[data-pg-paidcase]{order:0 !important}

  /* Same dynamic purple the gift pill has always had. */
  #cart#cart .pg-truegift-tag,
  body.template-cart .pg-truegift-tag{
    display:inline-block !important;
    background-image:linear-gradient(120deg,#9B4BC4 0%,#7A2FA2 30%,#4A1C66 50%,#7A2FA2 70%,#9B4BC4 100%) !important;
    background-size:240% 240% !important;
    animation:pgShift 5s ease-in-out infinite !important;
    color:#fff !important;
    -webkit-text-fill-color:#fff !important;
    font-size:12px !important;
    font-weight:700 !important;
    letter-spacing:.04em !important;
    padding:3px 10px !important;
    border-radius:999px !important;
    line-height:1.35 !important;
    white-space:nowrap !important;
    width:max-content !important;
    grid-area:sv !important;
    justify-self:start !important;
  }

  /* ---- 5. checkout pane sits on the bottom edge, not 40px above it ----
     The drawer's own bottom gutter is NOT set in CSS at all: pg-drawer's
     pgPane() writes it inline with !important every 800ms, so no stylesheet
     rule and no competing inline write can hold against it (both were tried
     and measured losing). It is changed at its single source, 34px -> 6px, in
     sections/pg-drawer.liquid. pg-cart-mobile's floorOf() reads that same
     value to decide whether CHECKOUT is reachable, so one owner is correct.
     This rule carries the safe-area inset INSIDE the pane, so a notched phone
     still clears its home indicator. 6 + 6 = a 12px resting gap. */
  aside#cart#cart .sticky-in-panel{
    padding-bottom:calc(6px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px)) !important;
  }
</style>
<script>
(function(){
  if (window.pgCaseTruth) return; window.pgCaseTruth = 1;

  var FREE = 49640846426340;   /* $0.00  "Free with console" */
  var PAID = 49640879063268;   /* $13.99 "Spare case"        */
  var LINES = '#cart .l4ca > li, body.template-cart .form-cart .l4ca > li';
  var TAG = '<span class="pg-truegift-tag">Free Gift</span>';

  /* The remove link is the only identifier that always survives: pg-theme-css
     strips product hrefs containing r36s-protective-case, but /cart/change
     carries no such substring. data-pg-keys (written by pg-cart-variants) is
     the backup, the product href the last resort. */
  function variantOf(li){
    var a = li.querySelector('a[href*="/cart/change"]');
    var m = a && (a.getAttribute('href') || '').match(/[?&]id=(\d+):/);
    if (m) return parseInt(m[1], 10);
    if (li.dataset.pgKeys){
      m = li.dataset.pgKeys.match(/^(\d+):/);
      if (m) return parseInt(m[1], 10);
    }
    a = li.querySelector('a[href*="/products/"]');
    m = a && (a.getAttribute('href') || '').match(/[?&]variant=(\d+)/);
    return m ? parseInt(m[1], 10) : 0;
  }

  function setText(el, txt){ if (el && el.textContent !== txt) el.textContent = txt; }

  /* The gift line: FREE GIFT pill, $0.00, no struck value, no save chip, and a
     quantity the shopper cannot push past one. */
  function asGift(li){
    delete li.dataset.pgPaidcase;      /* a line can flip variants when the cart is rebuilt */
    li.dataset.pgCase = '1';
    li.dataset.pgTruefree = '1';
    li.dataset.pgFree = '1';
    if (!li.querySelector('.pg-truegift-tag')){
      var h2 = li.querySelector('h2');
      if (h2) h2.insertAdjacentHTML('afterend', TAG);
    }
    /* "Free with console /" - the variant line, trailing separator and all,
       because the product's second option is unset on this variant. pg-drawer
       does hide it, but only via [data-pg-free] > section > p, so it appeared
       whenever this line lost the badge race to the paid case - which is the
       very failure being fixed here. Hidden inline as well as by the rule in
       4b, so it cannot come back on any ordering. The variant paragraph is the
       only unclassed direct <p> child of <section>; the price lives in .cols. */
    var sect = li.querySelector('section');
    if (sect){
      Array.prototype.forEach.call(sect.children, function(el){
        if (el.tagName === 'P' && !el.className) el.style.setProperty('display', 'none', 'important');
      });
    }
    setText(li.querySelector('.nc-lsave-now'), '$0.00');
    var p = li.querySelector('.cols p.price');
    if (p && !li.querySelector('.nc-lsave')) setText(p, '$0.00');
    /* opacity as well as visibility: pg-mobile's caseLine() re-writes
       visibility inline every 1200ms and would otherwise flash the stepper
       back on between our ticks (see 4b) */
    li.querySelectorAll('.semantic-amount').forEach(function(el){
      el.style.setProperty('visibility', 'hidden', 'important');
      el.style.setProperty('opacity', '0', 'important');
      el.style.setProperty('pointer-events', 'none', 'important');
    });
    var q = li.querySelector('input[name="updates[]"]');
    if (q && q.value !== '1') q.value = '1';
  }

  /* The paid line is an ordinary cart line. Everything the gift treatment adds
     is taken back off it, because two scripts still hand it that treatment
     whenever it happens to be the first case line in the cart. */
  function asPaid(li){
    li.dataset.pgCase = '1';
    li.dataset.pgPaidcase = '1';       /* CSS above benches any pill re-added between ticks */
    delete li.dataset.pgTruefree;
    delete li.dataset.pgFree;
    li.classList.remove('pg-free-line');
    /* our own pill is the one thing safe to remove: nothing else re-adds it */
    li.querySelectorAll('.pg-truegift-tag').forEach(function(el){
      if (el.parentNode) el.parentNode.removeChild(el);
    });
    li.querySelectorAll('.semantic-amount, .nc-lsave, .cols').forEach(function(el){
      el.style.setProperty('visibility', 'visible', 'important');
      el.style.removeProperty('opacity');
      el.style.removeProperty('pointer-events');
    });
  }

  /* "50% OFF today" (.pgx-tile-sub) rendered BELOW the "+ FREE Case" chip,
     where it read as an orphan line hanging off the bottom of the tile. The
     chip is markup INSIDE .pgx-tile-name, not a sibling, so no amount of CSS
     order can get the sub above it - the chip node itself is moved to sit
     after the sub. Idempotent, and re-run per tick because pg-landing and
     pg-tile-copy both rebuild these tiles from scratch on their own beats.
     Scoped away from .pgx-lad so the orb / wall-art ladders keep their own
     chip placement. */
  function subFirst(){
    document.querySelectorAll('#pgx .pgx-tile:not(.pgx-lad)').forEach(function(tile){
      var chip = tile.querySelector('.pgx-lad-chip');
      var sub = tile.querySelector('.pgx-tile-sub');
      if (!chip || !sub || !sub.parentNode) return;
      if (chip.previousElementSibling === sub) return;   /* already seated */
      /* the tiles are rebuilt underneath us; a node can be detached between
         the query and the move, which throws NotFoundError and would take the
         rest of the tick with it */
      try { sub.parentNode.insertBefore(chip, sub.nextSibling); } catch (e){}
    });
  }

  /* THE NOTE UNDER ADD TO CART. pg-tile-copy's noteFor() returns a real
     per-tier offer line on the orb / wall-art ladders, but on this product
     there is no PACK, so it falls through to one constant sentence that opens
     "Bundle pricing shown." - printed even when SINGLE is selected, where
     nothing is bundled and the sentence is simply not true. The rest of it is:
     a lone console is still discounted automatically at checkout (verified,
     /cart.js reports total_discount 649 on a 6499 line), so only the first
     sentence is dropped.

     Guarded twice so ladder products are never touched: it returns unless the
     note is that generic fallback, and it is self-correcting in both
     directions rather than latched on an attribute, so a repaint by
     pg-tile-copy is put back on the next tick. */
  var NOTE_SINGLE = 'Your <b>best available discount</b> is applied automatically at checkout.';
  var NOTE_BUNDLE = 'Bundle pricing shown. Your <b>best available discount</b> is applied automatically at checkout.';

  function dealNote(){
    var root = document.getElementById('pgx');
    if (!root) return;
    var p = root.querySelector('.pgx-deal-note');
    if (!p) return;
    var txt = (p.textContent || '').replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim();
    if (txt.indexOf('best available discount') === -1) return;   /* a real ladder offer line: leave it */
    var sel = root.querySelector('.pgx-lad.pgx-sel') || root.querySelector('.pgx-tile.pgx-sel');
    if (!sel) return;
    var single = sel.getAttribute('data-pgx-tile') === 'single' && !sel.classList.contains('pgx-duo');
    var bundleText = txt.indexOf('Bundle pricing shown') === 0;
    if (single && bundleText) p.innerHTML = NOTE_SINGLE;
    else if (!single && !bundleText) p.innerHTML = NOTE_BUNDLE;
  }

  /* Each step is isolated. A ReferenceError in one helper used to abort the
     whole tick, which silently disabled the cart fixes below it. */
  /* THE SINGLE TILE'S COMPARE-AT MUST FOLLOW THE SIZE PICKER.
     pg-theme-css builds .pgx-sstrike and the SAVE n% badge ONCE, from VARS[0]
     - the FIRST variant - and only ever updates them from a .pgx-storage
     <select> it synthesises for tiles that render option PILLS. This tile has
     a native <select data-pgx-size>, so `haveSel ? [] : pills` leaves pills
     empty, that whole branch never runs, and no updater is ever attached.
     Result, measured: picking 128G updated the price to $74.99 but left the
     64G compare-at struck beside it, so the tile read $129.99 -> $74.99 (42%)
     while its own badge said SAVE 50%. The 128G's real compare-at is $149.99.
     Showing another variant's compare-at is not a cosmetic problem, so this
     reads the figures live from the product JSON rather than hardcoding them,
     and an admin price change propagates with no further edit. */
  var VMAP = null, vmapPending = false;
  function loadVmap(){
    if (VMAP || vmapPending) return;
    var m = location.pathname.match(/\/products\/([^\/?#]+)/);
    if (!m) return;
    vmapPending = true;
    fetch('/products/' + m[1] + '.js')
      .then(function(r){ return r.json(); })
      .then(function(p){
        VMAP = (p.variants || []).map(function(v){
          return {title: String(v.title || ''), price: v.price, cap: v.compare_at_price || 0};
        });
      })
      .catch(function(){ vmapPending = false; });
  }
  function money(c){ return '$' + (c / 100).toFixed(2); }
  function strikeSync(){
    if (!VMAP){ loadVmap(); return; }
    var tile = document.querySelector('#pgx .pgx-tile[data-pgx-tile="single"]');
    if (!tile) return;
    var sel = tile.querySelector('select[data-pgx-size]');
    if (!sel) return;
    var want = String(sel.value || '').trim();
    if (!want) return;
    /* variant titles read "Transparent Purple / 64G"; the picker's value is
       the option segment, so compare on the last segment only */
    var v = null;
    for (var i = 0; i < VMAP.length; i++){
      if (VMAP[i].title.split('/').pop().trim() === want){ v = VMAP[i]; break; }
    }
    if (!v || !v.cap || v.cap <= v.price) return;
    setText(tile.querySelector('.pgx-sstrike'), money(v.cap));
    var bd = tile.querySelector('[data-pg-singlesave]') || tile.querySelector('.pgx-lad-badge');
    setText(bd, 'SAVE ' + Math.floor((v.cap - v.price) / v.cap * 100) + '%');
  }

  function pass(){
    try { subFirst(); } catch (e){}
    try { dealNote(); } catch (e){}
    try { strikeSync(); } catch (e){}
    document.querySelectorAll(LINES).forEach(function(li){
      var v = variantOf(li);
      if (v === FREE) asGift(li);
      else if (v === PAID) asPaid(li);
    });
  }

  /* One gift, one paid line. Extra gift units are moved onto the paid variant
     rather than deleted - pg-drawer attempts the same split with a variant id
     that 422s, so the units vanish instead of being charged for. */
  var busy = false;
  function normalise(){
    if (busy) return;
    busy = true;
    fetch('/cart.js', {headers: {'X-Requested-With': 'XMLHttpRequest'}})
      .then(function(r){ return r.json(); })
      .then(function(c){
        var gift = null;
        (c.items || []).forEach(function(it){ if (it.variant_id === FREE) gift = it; });
        if (!gift || gift.quantity <= 1){ busy = false; return; }
        var extra = gift.quantity - 1;
        return fetch('/cart/change.js', {
          method: 'POST', headers: {'Content-Type': 'application/json'},
          body: JSON.stringify({id: gift.key, quantity: 1})
        }).then(function(){
          return fetch('/cart/add.js', {
            method: 'POST', headers: {'Content-Type': 'application/json'},
            body: JSON.stringify({items: [{id: PAID, quantity: extra}]})
          });
        }).then(function(){
          busy = false;
          if (window.pgDrawerRefresh) window.pgDrawerRefresh();
        });
      })
      .catch(function(){ busy = false; });
  }

  /* THE REBUILD IS THE MOMENT THAT MATTERS. A Shipping Protection toggle
     replaces the drawer's entire innerHTML (pg-drawer spRefreshDrawer), and
     until this runs again the new nodes carry none of our stamps. Waiting for
     the next 250ms tick is what let pg-drawer's badge() and pg-mobile's
     caseLine() paint first. Observing #cart re-stamps in the same frame the
     nodes arrive.

     Re-entrancy: pass() writes to the DOM, which would re-trigger the
     observer, so the flag below drops anything raised by our own writes. The
     interval stays as the backstop for a drawer that is replaced wholesale
     (a new #cart element the observer is no longer attached to). */
  var stamping = false;
  function stamp(){
    if (stamping) return;
    stamping = true;
    try { pass(); } catch (e){}
    /* released after the current task so our own mutations are not read back
       as a reason to run again */
    setTimeout(function(){ stamping = false; }, 0);
  }
  function watchDrawer(){
    if (!window.MutationObserver) return;
    var c = document.getElementById('cart');
    if (!c || c.dataset.pgCaseWatch) return;
    c.dataset.pgCaseWatch = '1';
    new MutationObserver(stamp).observe(c, {childList: true, subtree: true});
  }

  /* Fast beat because the drawer replaces its own line nodes and pg-mobile
     re-badges by DOM order on its own interval; a one-shot guard loses. */
  setInterval(function(){ pass(); watchDrawer(); }, 250);
  setInterval(normalise, 2000);
  if (document.readyState === 'loading'){
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function(){ pass(); watchDrawer(); });
  } else {
    pass();
    watchDrawer();
  }
})();
</script>
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG Case Mobile + R36S Fix", "settings": []}
{% endschema %}
